# {{ meta.siteName }}

> Utsob Roy's digital garden: a public, evolving collection of musings, journal entries, essays, and reading notes on philosophy, religion, art, and technology, alongside technical how-tos and personal software projects.

This is a [digital garden](https://cagrimmett.com/notes/2020/11/08/what-are-digital-gardens/), not a blog: notes are living documents that keep changing, and each one carries a maturity marker (seedling, sapling, tree, withered, stone, signpost, or chest) noted near its title. A "seedling" is a half-formed thought; a "tree" is settled. See [{{ meta.siteBaseUrl }}/]({{ meta.siteBaseUrl }}/) for the full explanation of maturity levels. Contact: connect@utsob.me.

